- Centralizing specialist outcome ownership, bypassing owner authority gates, or requiring a provider-specific runtime in a task-wide lifecycle controller.
- Creating a separate Amọ̀ṣẹ́ repository before it has multiple independent skills or its own tooling and release lifecycle.
- Providing rigid generic templates for README, API, OpenAPI, changelog, or ADR documents.
- Adding a new public skill when an existing owner can express the recurring outcome cleanly.
